### Sample requests (VS Code "REST Client" extension or IntelliJ HTTP Client).
### Start the stack first: docker compose up --build
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. CREDIT approved -> 201, status EXECUTED, balanceAfter from the provider
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "acc-123456",
  "type": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 1500.00,
  "currency": "MXN",
  "description": "Transferencia recibida"
}

### 2. DEBIT rejected by the provider (INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS) -> 201, status REJECTED
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "acc-no-funds",
  "type": "DEBIT",
  "amount": 500.00,
  "currency": "MXN",
  "description": "Pago de servicios"
}

### 3. Account blocked (provider 403) -> 201, status REJECTED, failureCode ACCOUNT_BLOCKED
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "acc-blocked",
  "type": "DEBIT",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "MXN"
}

### 4. Provider error (500): retried 3 times -> 201, status FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "acc-provider-error",
  "type": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "MXN"
}

### 5. Provider too slow (read timeout): retried 3 times -> 201, status FAILED (takes ~10s)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "acc-slow",
  "type": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "MXN"
}

### 6. Business rule: amount must be > 1.00 -> 422 AMOUNT_TOO_LOW (provider not called)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "acc-123456",
  "type": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 1.00,
  "currency": "MXN"
}

### 7. Business rule: DEBIT max 10,000.00 -> 422 DEBIT_LIMIT_EXCEEDED
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "acc-123456",
  "type": "DEBIT",
  "amount": 10000.01,
  "currency": "MXN"
}

### 8. Business rule: only MXN -> 422 UNSUPPORTED_CURRENCY
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "acc-123456",
  "type": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 9. Invalid input -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR with every invalid field
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 10.555
}

### 10. Search: filters + pagination (page is 1-based, limit max 100)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?accountId=acc-123456&status=EXECUTED&type=CREDIT&page=1&limit=10

### 11. Search: everything, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions

### 12. Get by id (replace with an id from a previous response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 13. Health (includes the provider circuit breaker state)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### 14. Idempotency-Key, first time -> 201 (change the key to run it again from scratch)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-0001

{
  "accountId": "acc-123456",
  "type": "DEBIT",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "MXN",
  "description": "Pago con reintento"
}

### 15. Same Idempotency-Key and body again -> 200, Idempotent-Replayed: true, same id, provider not called
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-0001

{
  "accountId": "acc-123456",
  "type": "DEBIT",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "MXN",
  "description": "Pago con reintento"
}

### 16. Same Idempotency-Key, different amount -> 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-0001

{
  "accountId": "acc-123456",
  "type": "DEBIT",
  "amount": 300.00,
  "currency": "MXN",
  "description": "Pago con reintento"
}

### Swagger UI: http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html
